    "body": "blocked: the wrap-band fix is done and green, but the branch's own app-level verifier pin is red at the held commit - a pre-existing finding this run did not create\n\nFix landed: `band_trim` now reads the path's radial reach first and hands the base path on unchanged when the band covers the whole reach (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/radial_band.rs`, commit 815075be7 on `issue/2774-rotary-heights`, worktree `.claude/worktrees/issue-2774`). The read is clamped at 0 for the coverage check: a radius is a distance, and the retip read dips past the axis near it. `max(read, 0)` stays convex, so one ternary search reads the chord's low point. The span solve itself is untouched.\n\n- `a_band_that_wraps_the_whole_skin_adds_no_links`: green (hop-link parity, 88 = 88).\n- Full `camcraft-motion` rotary suite: 19 passed, 0 failed.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on `camcraft-motion` and `camcraft-app`: clean.\n\nQuick gate on the final head: 610 steps, 6 red.\n\n- `motion suites: rotary`: GREEN (the escalation's target).\n- 4 reds in code this branch never touches - `wire_taper_angle`, `ui suites: lib`, `import_step_curve_guard`, and the `app build` lane (link.exe exit 1318, a Windows linker flake). They cannot come from the band change; they are pre-existing on the machine or at the base.\n- 1 red is this issue's own pin: `rotary_verify::the_stated_radial_heights_move_the_generated_path`. It is red at the held commit 8f6e59d1e too - the earlier gate run counted it green against a stale build. The verifier finds `Envelope { at: 38, gouge_mm: 1.544, rest_mm: 0.096 }` on the banded parallel path (band 4.0..5.5, an r6 bar, ball d6): the tool cuts 1.54 mm below the model at one move. The verdict blocks the post, so the system refuses visibly - the Prime Directive holds - but the Done-means pin expects a clean verdict.\n\nWhat the gouge points at: the retip read `hypot(y, z + r) - r` is exact only where the skin's normal is the frame's radial direction (the crown). Where the skin slants, the kept stretch's real tool pose cuts deeper than the band's read believes. A fix is a re-read of the tip convention against the verifier's real-envelope law, and it changes posted G-code for every banded path - the same re-read the earlier comment called for. That is a new effort:max investigation, not a patch on this fix, so this run stops instead of forcing one.\n\nHeld work: commits 8f6e59d1e + 815075be7, unpushed, in the named worktree. The wrap fix is complete and pinned; the gouge pin is the open blocker for the PR.\n",
